{{also|discontinué|discontinúe}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|fro|descontinuer}}, equivalent to {{af|en|dis-|continue}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɪskənˈtɪnju/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-discontinue.ogg|a=US}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To interrupt the continuance of; to put an end to, especially as regards commercial productions; to stop [[producing]], [[making]], or [[supplying]].
#: {{ux|en|They plan to '''discontinue''' that design.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Merchant of Venice|III|iv|passage=I have '''discontinued''' school <br> Above a twelvemonth.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1603|author=w:Samuel Daniel|title=A Defence of Rime
|passage=Taught the Greek tongue, '''discontinued''' before in these parts the space of seven hundred years.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1669|author=w:William Holder|title=Elements of Speech
|passage=They modify and discriminate the voice, without appearing to '''discontinue''' it.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1946|month=January and February|title=Notes and News: Demolition of Rhydyfelin Viaduct|journal=Railway Magazine|page=52|text=Passenger traffic was subsequently '''discontinued''', and early in the recent war a considerable amount of the permanent way at the Treforest end of the railway was taken up.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2019-07-03|author=Mike D'Angelo|work=AV Club|title=Oscar Isaac and Ben Affleck blunder through a heavy heist in J.C. Chandor’s ''Triple Frontier''|url=https://film.avclub.com/oscar-isaac-and-ben-affleck-blunder-through-a-heavy-hei-1833123980|passage=Exactly 50 years ago, the U.S. Federal Reserve, which had previously issued bills with values as high as $10,000, made it all about the Benjamins. Every bill more valuable than $100 was officially '''discontinued'''. (They’d stopped being printed decades earlier, but many had kept circulating.)|accessdate=27 August 2020|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20191121211608/https://film.avclub.com/oscar-isaac-and-ben-affleck-blunder-through-a-heavy-hei-1833123980|archivedate=21 November 2019}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023-03-08|author=Gareth Dennis|title=The Reshaping of things to come...|journal=RAIL|issue=978|page=47|text=Beeching concludes, rather brutally, that "a high proportion of stopping passenger train services ought to be '''discontinued''' as soon as possible... and as soon as procedure permits".}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Jiachuan Wu and Ash Reynolds|title=As Trump aims to ax the penny, these are the coins that cost more than they're worth|magazine=w:NBC News|url=https://www.nbcnews.com/data-graphics/trump-aims-eliminate-penny-see-much-costs-produce-penny-nickel-rcna191739|date=2025-02-11|passage=If the penny is discontinued, it will join the ranks of other obsolete American coins, including the trime, a 3-cent coin '''discontinued''' in 1873, and the gold dollar coin, which was '''discontinued''' in 1889; that differed from the dollar coin currently in circulation.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To consciously cease the ingestion or administration of (a pharmaceutical drug).
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1989-04-08|journal=w:Gay Community News|page=3|author=Judy Harris|title=Fenway to Administer Peptide T|text=AZT, the only AIDS treatment fully approved by the Food and Drug Administration (FDA), is extremely toxic, and many people with AIDS cannot cake it or must '''discontinue''' taking it after some period of time.}}

